<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#ComponentCollection> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#ComponentCollection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#ComponentCollection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "component collection"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#ComponentCollection> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentComponent> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#ComponentCollection> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#ComponentCollection> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An instrument component whose identity is constituted by an organized collection of component members."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#ComponentMembership> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#ComponentMembership> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#ComponentMembership> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "component membership"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#ComponentMembership> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/core#IdentifiedResource> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#ComponentMembership> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#ComponentMembership> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A qualified, potentially time- and configuration-scoped relation between a parent component or instrument and a child component."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#ComponentMembership> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The membershipInstrument always names the overall instrument and childComponent names the member. When parentComponent is absent, the child is a direct member of the instrument rather than of another recorded component."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#FunctionalRoleAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#FunctionalRoleAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#FunctionalRoleAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "functional role assignment"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#FunctionalRoleAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/core#IdentifiedResource> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#FunctionalRoleAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#FunctionalRoleAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A contextual assignment of a governed functional-role concept to a component."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#FunctionalRoleAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The absence of a time, state, or configuration qualifier means that scope was not further specified; it does not prove that the role is permanent or universally applicable."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentComponent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "instrument component"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/core#Continuant> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentComponent> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A persistent physical, digital, or logical part that can participate in one or more instrument configurations."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentConfiguration> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentConfiguration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentConfiguration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "instrument configuration"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentConfiguration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/core#Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentConfiguration> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentConfiguration> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An arrangement of components, settings, and functional relationships applicable to an instrument or state."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentConfiguration> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "A configuration describes an arrangement. Its actual applicability is asserted through hasConfiguration or a qualified record scoped with appliesInConfiguration; configuration identity alone does not claim that the arrangement was active at every time."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentState> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "instrument state"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/core#Entity> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentState> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A time-scoped described condition of a musical instrument, distinct from the configurations that may apply during that condition."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Evidence for the recorded state may be attached through explicit assertions and evidence relations; state identity alone does not imply that evidence has been supplied."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#MusicalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#MusicalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#MusicalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "musical instrument"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#MusicalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/core#Continuant> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#MusicalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#MusicalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A continuant intentionally made, configured, or used to produce, control, or organize musical sound."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#MusicalInstrument> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Physical, electroacoustic, digital, virtual, and hybrid instruments may instantiate this class. A recording, model, package, or other representation of an instrument is not thereby the represented instrument."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#PlayingInterface> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#PlayingInterface> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#PlayingInterface> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "playing interface"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#PlayingInterface> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentComponent> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#PlayingInterface> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#PlayingInterface> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A component designed to mediate a performer’s interaction with an instrument; contextual use is represented separately by role assignment."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#appliesInConfiguration> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#appliesInConfiguration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#appliesInConfiguration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "applies in configuration"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#appliesInConfiguration> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentConfiguration> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#appliesInConfiguration> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#appliesInConfiguration> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Scopes a qualified relation, decision, or profile to an instrument configuration."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#appliesInConfiguration> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Memberships and functional-role assignments are the constrained 0.1.0 uses. No global domain is asserted so another explicitly governed qualified record can reuse the scoping relation without an incorrect type inference."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#appliesInState> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#appliesInState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#appliesInState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "applies in instrument state"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#appliesInState> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#InstrumentState> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#appliesInState> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#appliesInState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Scopes a membership, role assignment, configuration, or other qualified relation to an instrument state."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#appliesInState> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Memberships and functional-role assignments are the constrained 0.1.0 uses. The state must concern the same instrument as any accompanying configuration or membership-instrument qualifier."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#assignedRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#assignedRole> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#assignedRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#FunctionalRoleAssignment> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#assignedRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#assignedRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "assigned role"@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#assignedRole> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#assignedRole> <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "testing" .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#assignedRole> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Identifies the governed functional-role concept assigned to a component in context."@en .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#childComponent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#FunctionalProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/modavis/ontology/instrument#childComponent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
